    Datamunge::Rgb->new($red, $green, $blue, $opacity);

Construct the default opaque dark-slate ink color.

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::graphics::RGB>.

B<Example>

See the RGB class example.

Overloads (C++ picks one by the arguments' types):

=over 4

=item *

C<Datamunge::Rgb-E<gt>new()>

=item *

C<Datamunge::Rgb-E<gt>new($red (integer), $green (integer), $blue (integer), $opacity (number) = 1.0)>

=item *

C<Datamunge::Rgb-E<gt>new($red (integer))>

=item *

C<Datamunge::Rgb-E<gt>new($red (integer), $green (integer))>

=item *

C<Datamunge::Rgb-E<gt>new($color (string))>

=item *

C<Datamunge::Rgb-E<gt>new($color (string or undef))>

=back

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$red> (integer | string | string or undef, optional)

Red channel, conventionally 0-255.

=item C<$green> (integer, optional)

Green channel, conventionally 0-255.

=item C<$blue> (integer, optional)

Blue channel, conventionally 0-255.

=item C<$opacity> (number, optional)

Alpha in [0, 1], default 1 (opaque).

=back

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): For empty text, unknown names or malformed hex.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): For null, empty or malformed text.

=cut

