=head2 save

    $plot->save($path);

Writes the plot to C<path>, choosing the format from the file extension
(R's C<svg()>/C<png()>/C<pdf()> devices followed by C<dev.off()>, in one call).

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::graphics::Plot::save>.

C<.svg> or no extension writes the same text as to_svg(); C<.png> writes the raster image
the X11 viewer displays; C<.pdf> wraps that raster in a single-page PDF. The extension is
case-sensitive. An existing file is overwritten. Needs no display.

B<Example>

    auto plt = dm::Plot(dm::c(1.0, 2.0, 3.0), dm::c(1.0, 4.0, 9.0)).set_title("Squares");
    plt.save("squares.svg");  // vector
    plt.save("squares.png");  // raster
    plt.save("squares.pdf");  // raster in a one-page PDF

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$path> (string)

Destination file; relative paths resolve against the working directory.

=back

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): For any other extension (e.g. C<.jpg>).

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::runtime_error>): If the file cannot be opened for writing, the plot has no data series, or the canvas is smaller than its margins.

See also: C<save_svg()>, C<to_svg()>, C<show()>.

=cut

