    my $result = $r_plot->y_limits($min_y, $max_y);

Fixes the visible y range, like R's C<ylim = c(min_y, max_y)>.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::graphics::RPlot::y_limits>.

Without limits the y range is fitted to every layer, plus 10% padding at each end (bar
layers also include y = 0). With limits, the plotting area spans exactly
[C<min_y>, C<max_y>]. Data outside the range is not clipped.

B<Example>

See x_limits(), which sets both ranges.

