End x coordinates.

=item C<$y1> (array reference of number)

End y coordinates.

=item C<$color> (Datamunge::Rgb, optional)

Segment color (default opaque black).

=item C<$stroke_width> (number, optional)

Segment width in pixels (default 1).

=back

Returns Datamunge::RPlot: This plot, for chaining.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): If the four vectors differ in length or are empty.

See also: C<abline()>, C<polygon()>.

