package Datamunge::ImageLoader;

=head1 Datamunge::ImageLoader

A configurable, disk-backed batch iterator over a standard image dataset.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::datasets::ImageLoader>.

Datasets: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" (28x28 grayscale, 10 classes; 60000 train / 10000
test), "cifar10" (32x32 RGB, 10 classes; 50000 / 10000) and "cifar100" (32x32 RGB, 100 fine
or 20 coarse classes; 50000 / 10000).

Iteration works in epochs. has_next()/next() walk the current epoch's order; reset() starts
the next epoch (with a fresh shuffle when shuffling is on). Every setter returns the loader
for chaining and rewinds the current epoch, so configure before iterating.

Reading is const and opens files per call, so batch()/take() may be called from several
threads at once; next()/reset() and the setters mutate and must not race.

B<Example>

    dm::datasets::ImageLoader test("cifar10", "test");
    test.set_batch_size(500).set_layout("nchw").set_normalize(false);
    const auto first = test.next();          // shape {500, 3, 32, 32}, values 0..255
    std::print("{}\n", test.class_names()[first.labels[0]]);   // "cat"

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::ImageLoader->new($dataset, $split, $directory);

Opens a dataset split, downloading the files first if they are missing.

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::datasets::ImageLoader>.

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$split = 'train'>, C<$directory = ''>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$dataset> (string)

"mnist", "fashion_mnist", "cifar10" or "cifar100".

=item C<$split> (string, optional)

"train" or "test".

=item C<$directory> (string, optional)

Where the dataset's files are (or should be downloaded); empty means C<data_home() + "/" + dataset>.

=back

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): for an unknown dataset or split.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::runtime_error>): if the files are missing and cannot be downloaded, or are not valid files of that dataset.

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 890, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

