package Datamunge::BoundaryCondition1D;

=head1 Datamunge::BoundaryCondition1D

Owned endpoint data for Dirichlet, outward-conormal Neumann or Robin conditions.
Dirichlet uses value as u; Neumann uses it as p*du/dn; Robin uses it as the
reference value in p*du/dn+alpha*(u-value)=0. Alpha zero gives zero conormal.
For coercive diffusion/heat models use nonnegative Robin alpha and sufficient
constraints/reaction to remove the constant nullspace. Unsupported enum values
and nonfinite data are outside the solver's preconditions, not fully validated.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::fem::BoundaryCondition1D>.

B<Example>

    const dm::fem::BoundaryCondition1D right{dm::fem::BCType::Robin,4,3};
    std::print("{} {}\n",right.value,right.robin_coefficient); // 4 3

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

See also: L<Datamunge::Fem1D|/Datamunge::Fem1D>, L<Datamunge::BcType|/Datamunge::BcType>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::BoundaryCondition1D->new();

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::fem::BoundaryCondition1D>.

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 906, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 type

    my $value = $boundary_condition1_d->type;
    $boundary_condition1_d->type($value);

Supported condition kind; defaults to Dirichlet. (Datamunge::BcType constant).

=cut

sub type {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(900, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::call(901, [$self, $_[0]]);
    return;
}

=head2 value

    my $value = $boundary_condition1_d->value;
    $boundary_condition1_d->value($value);

Prescribed value, conormal or Robin reference, as selected by type. (number).

=cut

sub value {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(902, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::call(903, [$self, $_[0]]);
    return;
}

=head2 robin_coefficient

    my $value = $boundary_condition1_d->robin_coefficient;
    $boundary_condition1_d->robin_coefficient($value);

Robin alpha; ignored for other kinds. (number).

=cut

sub robin_coefficient {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(904, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::call(905, [$self, $_[0]]);
    return;
}

package Datamunge::Fem1DResult;

=head1 Datamunge::Fem1DResult

Owned nodal P1 steady solution, with checked scalar accessors for language bindings.
The continuous finite-element field is the piecewise-linear interpolant of
these values; nodal agreement alone does not imply agreement between nodes.
Copies own their arrays, with no mesh/callback alias. Public edits can break
array consistency; accessors check the actual requested vector bounds.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::fem::FEM1DResult>.

B<Example>

    const auto r=dm::fem::FEM1D::solve_builtin(dm::fem::make_uniform_mesh1d(0,1,2),{1},{0},"constant",{1},{},{});
    std::print("{} {}\n",r.size(),r.value_at(1)); // 3 0.125

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

See also: C<FEM1D::solve()>, C<algorithms::linear_interpolate()>.

