=head2 nearest

    my $result = $kd_tree2_d->nearest($query);

Return a nearest stored point under widened rounded hypot distance.
Equal computed distances prefer the earliest original input. O(n) worst
visited work/O(log n) recursion storage; no allocation/history/input copying.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::geometry::KDTree2D::nearest>.

B<Example>

    std::print("{}\n",dm::geometry::KDTree2D({{0,0},{2,0}}).nearest({1,0}).x); // 0

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$query> (Datamunge::Point2D)

Borrowed finite query, unchanged.

=back

Returns Datamunge::Point2D: Owned selected original coordinate, not a reference.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): On nonfinite query, even for an empty tree.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::logic_error>): On empty tree.

