=head2 k_nearest

    my $result = $kd_tree2_d->k_nearest($query, $k);

Return up to k closest coordinates, ordered by widened distance then original id.
Duplicate coordinates retain multiplicity. k=0/empty returns empty after finite
query validation. O(n log(min(k,n)+1)) worst work, O(k+log n) working storage.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::geometry::KDTree2D::k_nearest>.

B<Example>

    std::print("{}\n",dm::geometry::KDTree2D({{0,0},{2,0}}).k_nearest({1,0},5).size()); // 2

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$query> (Datamunge::Point2D)

Borrowed finite query.

=item C<$k> (integer)

Requested result count, clamped to tree size before heap use.

=back

Returns array reference of Datamunge::Point2D: Owned nearest-first coordinates, possibly fewer than k.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): On nonfinite query.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Arithmetic> (C++ C<std::overflow_error>): On nonfinite widened distance.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::bad_alloc>): On heap/result allocation failure.

