=head2 points_in_radius

    my $result = $kd_tree2_d->points_in_radius($query, $radius);

Return all stored coordinates with widened distanceE<lt>=radius, in tree traversal order.
Inclusive boundary, duplicate multiplicity. Negative/NaN radius rejects;
positive infinity includes every point without requiring a finite norm.
O(n) worst work, O(log n) recursion plus O(results) owned output.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::geometry::KDTree2D::points_in_radius>.

B<Example>

    std::print("{}\n",dm::geometry::KDTree2D({{0,0},{2,0}}).points_in_radius({1,0},1).size()); // 2

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$query> (Datamunge::Point2D)

Borrowed finite query, validated even for empty tree.

=item C<$radius> (number)

Nonnegative radius in coordinate units, positive infinity allowed.

=back

Returns array reference of Datamunge::Point2D: Owned matching coordinates, no guaranteed distance sorting.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): On nonfinite query or negative/NaN radius.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Arithmetic> (C++ C<std::overflow_error>): On nonfinite widened distance for a finite-radius query.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::bad_alloc>): On result allocation failure.

See also: C<k_nearest()>.

=cut

