package Datamunge::DifferentialEvolution;

=head1 Datamunge::DifferentialEvolution

DifferentialEvolution on the ArbitraryFunction callback interface.
Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.
The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws.
Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable
objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone
is not a uniform convergence certificate.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution>.

B<Example>

    const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
    std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500

B<References>

=over 4

=item *

R. Storn and K. Price (1997), Differential Evolution - A Simple and Efficient Heuristic for global Optimization over Continuous Spaces, https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1008202821328

=back

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

See also: L<Datamunge::DeOptions|/Datamunge::DeOptions>, C<trace_optimize()>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::DifferentialEvolution->new($options);

Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution>.

B<Example>

    const dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution optimizer;
    std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_generations); // 500

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$options = C++ default>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$options> (Datamunge::DeOptions, optional)

Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by DEOptions.

=back

See also: C<optimize()>.

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 1716, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 optimize

    my $result = $differential_evolution->optimize($function, \$coordinates, $lower_bound, $upper_bound);

Run DifferentialEvolution from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
Box-constrained differential mutation/crossover with greedy trial replacement. Supports the declared rand1/best1/current_to_best1/rand2 and binomial/exponential strategies. Coordinates seed one clamped member; more than twenty small-best-improvement generations can stop the run. O(population_size*p) storage; no global certificate.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::optimize>.

B<Example>

    dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
    dm::optim::DEOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
    std::vector<double> x{0,0};
    const auto value=dm::optim::DifferentialEvolution(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
    std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$function> (Datamunge::ArbitraryFunction)

Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.

=item C<$coordinates> (array reference of number, written back: pass a variable or a reference)

Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.

=item C<$lower_bound> (array reference of number)

Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.

=item C<$upper_bound> (array reference of number)

Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than lower limits.

=back

Returns number: Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): DifferentialEvolution::optimize: crossover_strategy must be 'binomial' or 'exponential'.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::exception>): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.

See also: C<trace_optimize()>, L<Datamunge::DeOptions|/Datamunge::DeOptions>.

=cut

sub optimize {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[2] = Datamunge::Rosetta::slot(0, $args[2]) if @args > 2;
    my %writebacks;
    my $result = Datamunge::Rosetta::call(1714, \@args, \%writebacks);
    Datamunge::Rosetta::write_back(\@_, 2, $writebacks{0}) if exists $writebacks{0};
    return $result;
}

=head2 options

    my $result = $differential_evolution->options();

Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::DifferentialEvolution::options>.

Returns Datamunge::DeOptions: Const option reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.

=cut

sub options {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(1715, [@_]);
}

