package Datamunge::FireflyAlgorithm;

=head1 Datamunge::FireflyAlgorithm

The Firefly Algorithm (Yang, 2008/2009): a population of fireflies is pairwise
attracted toward brighter (better) neighbors, with attractiveness decaying with
squared distance and a shrinking random-walk term for exploration. Derivative-free,
O(n^2) per iteration in the population size.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm>.

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::FireflyAlgorithm->new($options);

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm>.

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$options = C++ default>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$options> (Datamunge::FireflyAlgorithmOptions, optional)

=back

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 1772, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 optimize

    my $result = $firefly_algorithm->optimize($function, \$coordinates, $lower_bound, $upper_bound);

Minimizes C<function> within [C<lower_bound>, C<upper_bound>], updating
C<coordinates> in place to the best point found, and returns its value. The
initial C<coordinates> (clamped into bounds) seed one member of the population.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm::optimize>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$function> (Datamunge::ArbitraryFunction)

=item C<$coordinates> (array reference of number, written back: pass a variable or a reference)

=item C<$lower_bound> (array reference of number)

=item C<$upper_bound> (array reference of number)

=back

Returns number.

=cut

sub optimize {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[2] = Datamunge::Rosetta::slot(0, $args[2]) if @args > 2;
    my %writebacks;
    my $result = Datamunge::Rosetta::call(1770, \@args, \%writebacks);
    Datamunge::Rosetta::write_back(\@_, 2, $writebacks{0}) if exists $writebacks{0};
    return $result;
}

=head2 options

    my $result = $firefly_algorithm->options();

The options this FireflyAlgorithm was configured with.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::FireflyAlgorithm::options>.

Returns Datamunge::FireflyAlgorithmOptions: The stored options.

=cut

sub options {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(1771, [@_]);
}

