=head2 optimize

    my $result = $genetic_algorithm->optimize($function, \$coordinates, $lower_bound, $upper_bound);

Run GeneticAlgorithm from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
Real-valued box-constrained selection, crossover, Gaussian mutation and optional elitism. Initial coordinates seed a clamped population member. Returns the best member of the final population. Retaining at least one elite ensures that this member ties the best visited loss. The solver can stop after more than twenty small-best-improvement generations. O(population_size*p) storage; strategy/rate choices affect results, with no global certificate.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::GeneticAlgorithm::optimize>.

B<Example>

    dm::optim::QuadraticObjective f({2,8},{1,-2});
    dm::optim::GAOptions controls;controls.max_generations=5;
    std::vector<double> x{0,0};
    const auto value=dm::optim::GeneticAlgorithm(controls).optimize(f,x,std::vector<double>{-3,-3},std::vector<double>{3,3});
    std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$function> (Datamunge::ArbitraryFunction)

Borrowed ArbitraryFunction with matching finite output shapes.

=item C<$coordinates> (array reference of number, written back: pass a variable or a reference)

Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.

=item C<$lower_bound> (array reference of number)

Matching finite inclusive lower box limits.

=item C<$upper_bound> (array reference of number)

Matching finite inclusive upper limits, greater than lower limits.

=back

Returns number: Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): GeneticAlgorithm::optimize: population_size must be at least 2.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::exception>): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.

See also: C<trace_optimize()>, L<Datamunge::GaOptions|/Datamunge::GaOptions>.

=cut

