Run InteriorPoint from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
Gradient steps on f-mu*sum(log(-c)) with cE<lt>0. Backtracks only for strict feasibility, not barrier-objective decrease, then decays mu after each fixed inner budget. Requires a strictly feasible start and can fail later when feasible steps underflow. No KKT or barrier-stationarity stop test; no phase-I feasibility search.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::InteriorPoint::optimize>.

B<Example>

    dm::optim::NonnegativeQuadratic f({-1,2});
