package Datamunge::Sgd;

=head1 Datamunge::Sgd

SGD on the DifferentiableSeparableFunction callback interface.
Uses the mean gradient of each mini-batch, reshuffling component indices each epoch when enabled. Full objective remains the sum of components. Stops on absolute full-objective change per epoch. Nonempty components and positive batch_size are required; seeds reproduce the same build, not a cross-library shuffle transcript.
The caller supplies finite, dimensionally consistent callbacks. Inputs are borrowed;
coordinates mutate in place and can retain a partial state if a callback throws.
Calls use local optimizer state and propagate callback exceptions; sharing a mutable
objective across threads requires external synchronisation. Normal return alone
is not a uniform convergence certificate.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::optim::SGD>.

B<Example>

    const dm::optim::SGD optimizer;
    std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_epochs); // 100

B<References>

=over 4

=item *

H. Robbins and S. Monro (1951), A Stochastic Approximation Method, https://doi.org/10.1214/aoms/1177729586. The fixed-rate reshuffling variant here differs from their decreasing-step stochastic approximation.

=back

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

See also: L<Datamunge::SgdOptions|/Datamunge::SgdOptions>, C<trace_optimize()>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::Sgd->new($options);

Store a copy of the controls without running the objective.

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::optim::SGD>.

B<Example>

    const dm::optim::SGD optimizer;
    std::print("{}\n",optimizer.options().max_epochs); // 100

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$options = C++ default>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$options> (Datamunge::SgdOptions, optional)

Method-specific controls; defaults are listed by SGDOptions.

=back

See also: C<optimize()>.

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 2101, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 optimize

    my $result = $sgd->optimize($function, \$coordinates);

Run SGD from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
Uses the mean gradient of each mini-batch, reshuffling component indices each epoch when enabled. Full objective remains the sum of components. Stops on absolute full-objective change per epoch. Nonempty components and positive batch_size are required; seeds reproduce the same build, not a cross-library shuffle transcript.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::SGD::optimize>.

B<Example>

    dm::optim::LeastSquaresObjective f({{1},{1}},{1,3});
    dm::optim::SGDOptions controls;controls.max_epochs=5;
    std::vector<double> x{0};
    const auto value=dm::optim::SGD(controls).optimize(f,x);
    std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$function> (Datamunge::DifferentiableSeparableFunction)

Borrowed DifferentiableSeparableFunction with matching finite output shapes.

=item C<$coordinates> (array reference of number, written back: pass a variable or a reference)

Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.

=back

Returns number: Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): SGD: batch_size must be positive; SGD::optimize: function has zero terms.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::exception>): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.

See also: C<trace_optimize()>, L<Datamunge::SgdOptions|/Datamunge::SgdOptions>.

=cut

sub optimize {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[2] = Datamunge::Rosetta::slot(0, $args[2]) if @args > 2;
    my %writebacks;
    my $result = Datamunge::Rosetta::call(2099, \@args, \%writebacks);
    Datamunge::Rosetta::write_back(\@_, 2, $writebacks{0}) if exists $writebacks{0};
    return $result;
}

=head2 options

    my $result = $sgd->options();

Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::SGD::options>.

Returns Datamunge::SgdOptions: Const option reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.

=cut

sub options {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(2100, [@_]);
}

