sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 2141, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 optimize

    my $result = $svrg->optimize($function, \$coordinates);

Run SVRG from the supplied point using the configured finite budget.
Uses mean component gradients: current_i-snapshot_i+full_snapshot_gradient/n. The division by n is essential for an unbiased mean-loss estimator and matches SGD/SAGA scale. Earlier code omitted it. Stops on absolute full-sum objective change per epoch. O(p) snapshot state, two component-gradient calls per inner update plus one full gradient per epoch.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::SVRG::optimize>.

B<Example>

    dm::optim::LeastSquaresObjective f({{1},{1}},{1,3});
    dm::optim::SVRGOptions controls;controls.max_epochs=5;
    std::vector<double> x{0};
    const auto value=dm::optim::SVRG(controls).optimize(f,x);
    std::print("{}\n",std::isfinite(value)); // true

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$function> (Datamunge::DifferentiableSeparableFunction)

Borrowed DifferentiableSeparableFunction with matching finite output shapes.

=item C<$coordinates> (array reference of number, written back: pass a variable or a reference)

Owned-by-caller finite start; overwritten with the native returned point.

=back

Returns number: Objective at the native returned coordinates; not a stop-status code.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): SVRG: step_size must be positive; SVRG: tolerance must be non-negative; SVRG: function has zero terms.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::exception>): Exceptions from supplied callbacks propagate. Raw solvers do not uniformly reject nonfinite inputs.

See also: C<trace_optimize()>, L<Datamunge::SvrgOptions|/Datamunge::SvrgOptions>.

=cut

sub optimize {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[2] = Datamunge::Rosetta::slot(0, $args[2]) if @args > 2;
    my %writebacks;
    my $result = Datamunge::Rosetta::call(2139, \@args, \%writebacks);
    Datamunge::Rosetta::write_back(\@_, 2, $writebacks{0}) if exists $writebacks{0};
    return $result;
}

=head2 options

    my $result = $svrg->options();

Borrow this optimizer's stored configuration.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::optim::SVRG::options>.

Returns Datamunge::SvrgOptions: Const option reference, valid during this object's lifetime; no mutation.

=cut

sub options {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(2140, [@_]);
}

