=head2 psi_weights

    my $result = $arima->psi_weights($count);

The first C<count>

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::stats::ARIMA::psi_weights>.

C<\psi>-weights of the full model, differencing included:
C<y_t=\sum_{j\ge0}\psi_j\varepsilon_{t-j}> formally, with C<\psi_0=1>.

The h-step forecast error is C<\sum_{jE<lt>h}\psi_j\varepsilon_{t+h-j}>, so its variance is
C<\sigma^2\sum_{jE<lt>h}\psi_j^2>; forecast_with_intervals() uses exactly these weights.

C<\psi_0,\dots,\psi_{count-1}>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$count> (integer)

Number of weights.

=back

Returns array reference of number.

=cut

