    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 2354, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

package Datamunge::BSplineRegression;

=head1 Datamunge::BSplineRegression

A least-squares B-spline regression curve y ≈ Σ_j β_j B_j(x). C<dm::BSR> for short.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::BSplineRegression>.

The fit is ordinary least squares (no roughness penalty). Throws std::invalid_argument for
mismatched/empty inputs or too few basis functions for the degree, and std::runtime_error when
the design is rank deficient (some basis function has too little data under it; use fewer
basis functions / knots).

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::BSplineRegression->new($x, $y, $n_basis, $degree);

Fixed-width basis: C<n_basis> B-splines of the given C<degree> (cubic by default)
whose knots are equally spaced over the range of C<x>.

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::BSplineRegression>.

Overloads (C++ picks one by the arguments' types):

=over 4

=item *

C<Datamunge::BSplineRegression-E<gt>new($x (array reference), $y (array reference), $n_basis (integer), $degree (integer) = 3)>

=item *

C<Datamunge::BSplineRegression-E<gt>new($x (array reference), $y (array reference), $knots (array reference), $degree (integer) = 3)>

=back

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$x> (array reference)

=item C<$y> (array reference)

=item C<$n_basis> (integer | array reference)

=item C<$degree> (integer, optional)

=back

=cut

