Uses one color for all points and clears any grouping.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::Splom::color>.

Clears group_by(), point_colors(), and the factor form of set_col().

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$value> (Datamunge::Rgb)

Point color (default C<{37, 99, 235}>).

=back

Returns Datamunge::Splom: This matrix, for chaining.

See also: C<set_col(datamunge::graphics::RGB)>.

=cut

sub color {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(2495, [@_]);
