package Datamunge::Dual;

=head1 Datamunge::Dual

SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::Dual -- a first-order forward-mode
dual number. Build an expression out of named operations (starting from a seed
with derivative=1) to read off an exact derivative alongside the value.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::Dual>.

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::Dual->new($value, $derivative);

A dual number value + derivative·ε (ε² = 0).

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::Dual>.

Seed the variable you differentiate with derivative 1 and constants with 0; every
operation then carries the exact derivative with respect to that seed.

B<Example>

    const dm::Dual x(2.0, 1.0);  // seed d/dx
    std::print("{}\n", x.multiply(x).derivative());  // 4

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$derivative = 0.0>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$value> (number)

Real part, the function value.

=item C<$derivative> (number, optional)

Dual part, the derivative with respect to the seed (default 0).

=back

=cut

