package Datamunge::Tape;

=head1 Datamunge::Tape

SWIG-friendly facade for datamunge::autodiff::Tape -- a reverse-mode
("backpropagation") computation tape. Create leaf Vars against a Tape, build an
expression out of named Var operations, then call backward() on the output Var
to get the derivative of that output with respect to every node on the tape
(index a leaf's own index() into the result to read its gradient).

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::Tape>.

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::Tape->new();

An empty tape; create leaf Vars against it with Var(tape, value).

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::Tape>.

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 3267, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 size

    my $result = $tape->size();

Number of recorded nodes (leaves plus operation results).

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::Tape::size>.

Returns integer.

=cut

sub size {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3264, [@_]);
}

=head2 value_at

    my $result = $tape->value_at($index);

The value recorded at node C<index>.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::Tape::value_at>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$index> (integer)

Node index, as returned by Var::index().

=back

Returns number: The node's value.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::OutOfRange> (C++ C<std::out_of_range>): When C<index> E<gt>= size().

=cut

sub value_at {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3265, [@_]);
}

=head2 backward

    my $result = $tape->backward($output);

Reverse sweep from C<output>: d(output)/d(node) for every node on the tape.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::Tape::backward>.

The tape is unchanged, so backward() may be called again for other outputs.

B<Example>

    dm::Tape tape;
    const dm::Var a(tape, 2.0), b(tape, 3.0);
    const auto grad = tape.backward(a.multiply(b));
    std::print("{} {}\n", grad[a.index()], grad[b.index()]);  // 3 2

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$output> (Datamunge::Var)

A Var recorded on this tape (usually the final expression).

=back

Returns array reference of number: One adjoint per node, indexed by Var::index() (0-based; add 1 in R and Lua).

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::OutOfRange> (C++ C<std::out_of_range>): When C<output> is not a node of this tape.

=cut

sub backward {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3266, [@_]);
}

package Datamunge::MlpClassifierSearch;

=head1 Datamunge::MlpClassifierSearch

A two-predictor MLP classifier with Bayesian hidden-width selection and a held-out test.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::MLPClassifierSearch>.

Splits complete labelled data by class into 60% fitting, 20% validation and 20%
test rows (per-class rounding applies). Four random widths followed by eight
Gaussian-process expected-improvement proposals are the default search budget.
Proposals in [min_hidden,max_hidden] are rounded to integer widths; repeated
widths reuse their cached validation log loss. Smaller loss wins; ties retain
the first proposal. Each candidate has one tanh hidden layer, softmax output,
training-only standardization, SGD learning rate 0.05, batch size 32 and L2
penalty 0.0001. Initialization/shuffling use seed for every candidate.

After selection the network is refitted on fitting plus validation rows,
with new standardization statistics, then scored once on the untouched test.
Validation loss belongs to the candidate fit, not the final refit, and is an
optimistic selection score. Neither split nor test performance is a guarantee
for other seeds or datasets. Owns all state, borrows inputs only during calls,
does not change data or global RNG state. Const methods may run concurrently.
Search cost is at most (initial_samples+iterations) fits plus one refit;
cached repeats are cheaper. Prediction/plot costs follow MLPClassifier.

B<Example>

    const std::unique_ptr<dm::DataFrame> iris(dm::data::iris());
    dm::MLPClassifierSearch fit(*iris, "Species", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width");
    const bool valid = fit.best_hidden_nodes() >= 2 && fit.best_hidden_nodes() <= 24; // true

B<References>

=over 4

=item *

D. R. Jones, M. Schonlau and W. J. Welch (1998), Efficient Global Optimization
of Expensive Black-Box Functions, https://doi.org/10.1023/A:1008306431147

=back

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

See also: C<stats::MLPClassifier>, C<optim::BayesianOptimization>, C<stats::train_test_split()>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::MlpClassifierSearch->new($data, $response, $x_feature, $y_feature, $min_hidden, $max_hidden, $initial_samples, $iterations, $epochs, $seed);

Tune a single hidden layer, refit on development rows and evaluate the test rows.

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::MLPClassifierSearch>.

B<Example>

    const std::unique_ptr<dm::DataFrame> iris(dm::data::iris());
    dm::MLPClassifierSearch fit(*iris, "Species", "Petal.Length", "Petal.Width", 2, 24, 4, 8, 400, 42);
    const auto n = fit.test_rows(); // 30

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$min_hidden = 2>, C<$max_hidden = 24>, C<$initial_samples = 4>, C<$iterations = 8>, C<$epochs = 400>, C<$seed = 42>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$data> (Datamunge::DataFrame)

Borrowed labelled frame; unchanged. Every selected value must be present and finite.

=item C<$response> (string)

String response column, with nonempty labels and at least five rows per class.

=item C<$x_feature> (string)

First numeric predictor, distinct from response and y_feature.

=item C<$y_feature> (string)

Second numeric predictor; these two are the only model inputs.

=item C<$min_hidden> (integer, optional)

Smallest hidden width, default 2; at least 1 and below max_hidden.

=item C<$max_hidden> (integer, optional)

Largest hidden width, default 24; at most 1000000.

=item C<$initial_samples> (integer, optional)

Random initial proposals, default 4; at least 1.

=item C<$iterations> (integer, optional)

Surrogate-guided proposals, default 8; zero permits initial design only.

=item C<$epochs> (integer, optional)

SGD passes for each candidate and the final refit, default 400; at least 1.

=item C<$seed> (integer, optional)

Local split/search/initialization seed, default 42; validation split uses seed+1 modulo 2^64.

=back

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): For invalid columns, labels, nonfinite/missing data or search controls.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::runtime_error>): If fitting or scoring fails to produce finite probabilities.

See also: L<Datamunge::MlpClassifierSearch|/Datamunge::MlpClassifierSearch>, C<summary()>.

=cut

