package Datamunge::TaskOutput;

=head1 Datamunge::TaskOutput

Preallocated observations, rewards and independent episode-end flags.
Observations are row-major [environments,observation_size]. Terminal observations
stay in final_observations until the next terminal transition for that index.
No auto-reset occurs. Masked-out rows keep all previous values.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::sim::TaskOutput>.

B<Example>

    dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::InvertedPendulum,2);
    const auto& result=task.output();

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

    Datamunge::TaskOutput->new();

Calls the C++ constructor C<datamunge::sim::TaskOutput>.

=cut

sub new {
    my $class = shift;
    my $self = bless {}, ref($class) || $class;
    my @args = @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::construct($self, 3514, 0, \@args);
    return $self;
}

=head2 observations

    my $value = $task_output->observations;

Current observations, including terminal states. (array reference of number, read-only).

=cut

sub observations {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3502, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::binding_error('Datamunge::TaskOutput::observations is read-only');
}

=head2 rewards

    my $value = $task_output->rewards;

Reward from the last selected step, zero after reset. (array reference of number, read-only).

=cut

sub rewards {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3504, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::binding_error('Datamunge::TaskOutput::rewards is read-only');
}

=head2 terminated

    my $value = $task_output->terminated;

Physical failure, requiring explicit reset. (byte string or array reference of integers, read-only).

=cut

sub terminated {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3506, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::binding_error('Datamunge::TaskOutput::terminated is read-only');
}

=head2 truncated

    my $value = $task_output->truncated;

Time limit, requiring explicit reset; bootstrap is valid. (byte string or array reference of integers, read-only).

=cut

sub truncated {
    my $self = shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3508, [$self]) unless @_;
    Datamunge::Rosetta::binding_error('Datamunge::TaskOutput::truncated is read-only');
}

