package Datamunge::TaskBatch;

=head1 Datamunge::TaskBatch

Batched native InvertedPendulum or Hopper rollouts without a graphics dependency.
CPU worlds use persistent parallel workers. Actions and all output arrays are
finite double precision, with no NN dependency. Single-writer, including reset.
Invalid actions fail before forces are applied. A native solver error propagates;
reset selected worlds before retrying after such an error. Reset uses small
independent uniform joint perturbations and never touches another row's RNG.

Wraps the C++ class C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch>.

B<Example>

    dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::InvertedPendulum,4,dm::compute::Context({},2),42);
    const auto& result=task.step(std::vector<double>(4,0));

Inherits from L<Datamunge::NativeObject|/Datamunge::NativeObject>.

=cut

our @ISA = ('Datamunge::NativeObject');

=head2 new

There is no public C++ constructor: C++ functions return the objects of Datamunge::TaskBatch.

=cut

sub new { Datamunge::Rosetta::binding_error('Datamunge::TaskBatch has no public C++ constructor: C++ functions return its objects') }

=head2 size

    my $result = $task_batch->size();

Return the number of independent environments.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::size>.

Returns integer: Positive environment count.

=cut

sub size {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3515, [@_]);
}

=head2 observation_size

    my $result = $task_batch->observation_size();

Read the task's observation width.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::observation_size>.

Returns integer: Four for InvertedPendulum or eleven for Hopper.

=cut

sub observation_size {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3516, [@_]);
}

=head2 action_size

    my $result = $task_batch->action_size();

Read the continuous action width.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::action_size>.

Returns integer: One for InvertedPendulum or three for Hopper.

=cut

sub action_size {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3517, [@_]);
}

=head2 output

    my $result = $task_batch->output();

Borrow current rollout outputs without advancing the simulation.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::output>.

Returns Datamunge::TaskOutput: Internal reusable arrays, valid until destruction and modified by step/reset.

=cut

sub output {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3518, [@_]);
}

=head2 step

    my $result = $task_batch->step($actions, $mask);

Advance selected task rows and retain final observations on episode end.
Selected completed rows must be reset first. An unselected row remains unchanged.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::step>.

B<Example>

    dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::Hopper,1);
    const auto& result=task.step({0,0,0});

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$mask = C++ default>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$actions> (array reference of number)

Row-major [size(),action_size()] values in the documented action box.

=item C<$mask> (byte string or array reference of integers, optional)

Empty selects all; otherwise size() binary bytes.

=back

Returns Datamunge::TaskOutput: Borrowed reusable rollout output; no automatic reset.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): Invalid action shape/value or mask, before mutation.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::logic_error>): A selected row already finished.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::exception>): Physics failure; explicit reset is required before retrying.

=cut

sub step {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[2] = Datamunge::Rosetta::bytes($args[2]) if @args > 2;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3519, \@args);
}

=head2 reset

    my $result = $task_batch->reset($mask);

Restore and perturb selected rows; retain final observations for rollout collectors.
Clears rewards/end flags for selected rows. Random streams continue between episodes.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::reset>.

B<Example>

    dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::InvertedPendulum,2);task.reset({0,1});

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$mask = C++ default>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$mask> (byte string or array reference of integers, optional)

Empty selects all; otherwise size() binary bytes.

=back

Returns Datamunge::TaskOutput: Borrowed reset observations and current unselected rows.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): Invalid mask.

=cut

sub reset {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[1] = Datamunge::Rosetta::bytes($args[1]) if @args > 1;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3520, \@args);
}

=head2 seed

    $task_batch->seed($seed);

Reproduce fresh reset draws after explicit reseeding; physics is unchanged until reset.

Calls the C++ method C<datamunge::sim::TaskBatch::seed>.

B<Example>

    dm::sim::TaskBatch task(dm::sim::Task::Hopper,1);task.seed(7);task.reset();

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$seed> (integer)

New batch random seed.

=back

=cut

sub seed {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3521, [@_]);
}

=head2 create

    my $result = Datamunge::TaskBatch->create($task, $count, $workers, $seed, $time_limit);

Create an owned native CPU task batch. task is InvertedPendulum or Hopper; count and workers
must be positive. seed defaults to zero and time_limit to 1000 successful episode steps.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::perl_bindings::task_batch_create>.

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$workers = 1>, C<$seed = 0>, C<$time_limit = 1000>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$task> (Datamunge::Task constant)

=item C<$count> (integer)

=item C<$workers> (integer, optional)

=item C<$seed> (integer, optional)

=item C<$time_limit> (integer, optional)

=back

Returns Datamunge::TaskBatch or undef.

=cut

sub create {
    shift;
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(3522, [@_]);
}

