=over 4

=item C<$f> (Datamunge::Expr)

=item C<$var> (string)

=item C<$center> (number)

=item C<$order> (integer)

=back

Returns Datamunge::Polynomial.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): if order is negative, or std::invalid_argument propagated from Expr::differentiate() if f contains a non-constant exponent.

=cut

