=head2 hmc_proposal

    my $result = hmc_proposal($log_posterior, $position, $momentum, $step_size, $num_steps);

Integrate one HMC proposal with fixed step size and caller-provided momentum.
The mass matrix is the identity. The caller can apply the Metropolis
correction by accepting when log(uniform) is less than -energy_change.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::bayes::hmc_proposal>.

    dm::bayes::AutodiffModel density([](auto&, const auto& q) { return -.5 * q[0] * q[0]; });
    auto proposal = dm::bayes::hmc_proposal(density, {1.0}, {0.0}, .1, 10);

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$log_posterior> (Datamunge::DifferentiableFunction)

Differentiable log density, up to an additive constant.

=item C<$position> (array reference of number)

Finite initial position on the unconstrained scale.

=item C<$momentum> (array reference of number)

Finite initial momentum with the same dimension.

=item C<$step_size> (number)

Positive finite leapfrog step size.

=item C<$num_steps> (integer)

Positive number of leapfrog steps.

=back

Returns Datamunge::HmcProposal: Proposed position and momentum and their signed energy change. Nonfinite proposed energy is reported as computed for divergence diagnostics.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): Invalid dimensions, inputs or step size.

See also: L<Datamunge::Hmc|/Datamunge::Hmc>, C<leapfrog_gaussian_acceptance()>.

=cut

