Harris corner detection: response = det(M) - k*trace(M)^2 of the structure tensor M
at every pixel, thresholded at C<threshold_ratio> * (the response map's own max, so
callers don't have to guess an absolute scale) and non-max-suppressed within a
(2*nms_radius+1)^2 window. C<k> is the classical Harris free parameter (0.04-0.06).

Calls C++ C<datamunge::cv::harris_corners>.

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$k = 0.04>, C<$sigma = 1.0>, C<$threshold_ratio = 0.01>, C<$nms_radius = 3>.

