=over 4

=item C<$line> (Datamunge::HoughLine)

=item C<$image_width> (integer)

=item C<$image_height> (integer)

=item C<$p1> (array reference [integer, integer], written back: pass a variable or a reference)

=item C<$p2> (array reference [integer, integer], written back: pass a variable or a reference)

=back

Returns boolean.

=cut

sub line_endpoints {
    my @args = @_;
    $args[3] = Datamunge::Rosetta::slot(0, $args[3]) if @args > 3;
    $args[4] = Datamunge::Rosetta::slot(1, $args[4]) if @args > 4;
    my %writebacks;
    my $result = Datamunge::Rosetta::call(79, \@args, \%writebacks);
    Datamunge::Rosetta::write_back(\@_, 3, $writebacks{0}) if exists $writebacks{0};
    Datamunge::Rosetta::write_back(\@_, 4, $writebacks{1}) if exists $writebacks{1};
    return $result;
}

=head2 hough_lines

    my $result = hough_lines($img, $edge_threshold, $min_votes, $nms_radius);

Standard Hough line transform: every pixel of C<img> whose grayscale luma is E<gt>= C<edge_threshold>
votes, in a rho-theta accumulator (theta stepped every degree over
[0, pi), rho stepped every pixel over the image's diagonal range), for every line
that could pass through it. Returns every accumulator cell with at least C<min_votes>,
non-max-suppressed within a (2*nms_radius+1) rho-theta cell window so a
single real line doesn't produce a cluster of near-duplicate near-identical results.
Intended input is an edge map (e.g. image::sobel_edges()'s output), not a raw photo.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::cv::hough_lines>.

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$edge_threshold = 128>, C<$min_votes = 50>, C<$nms_radius = 5>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$img> (Datamunge::Image)

=item C<$edge_threshold> (integer, optional)

=item C<$min_votes> (integer, optional)

=item C<$nms_radius> (integer, optional)

=back

Returns array reference of Datamunge::HoughLine.

=cut

sub hough_lines {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(80, [@_]);
}

=head2 hough_circles

    my $result = hough_circles($img, $min_radius, $max_radius, $gradient_threshold, $min_votes, $nms_radius);

Gradient-direction-guided Hough circle transform: for every edge pixel (Sobel
gradient magnitude E<gt>= C<gradient_threshold> on C<img's> grayscale conversion), and
for every candidate radius in [C<min_radius>, C<max_radius>], votes for the two
candidate centers at that distance along the pixel's gradient line (handles both
bright-disk-on-dark and dark-disk-on-bright edge polarity). Each radius gets an
independent 2D (cx, cy) accumulator and non-max suppression pass -- simpler to
reason about than a combined 3D (cx, cy, r) accumulator, at the cost of not
suppressing near-duplicate detections across adjacent radii.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::cv::hough_circles>.

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$gradient_threshold = 5e+01>, C<$min_votes = 20>, C<$nms_radius = 10>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$img> (Datamunge::Image)

=item C<$min_radius> (integer)

=item C<$max_radius> (integer)

=item C<$gradient_threshold> (number, optional)

=item C<$min_votes> (integer, optional)

=item C<$nms_radius> (integer, optional)

=back

Returns array reference of Datamunge::HoughCircle.

=cut

sub hough_circles {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(81, [@_]);
}

