=head2 fetch

    my $result = fetch($name, $directory);

Makes sure a downloadable dataset is on disk and returns where it is.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::datasets::fetch>.

For tabular datasets this is the CSV file. UCI names such as "uci_53"
and "uci_iris" point to the same cache. UCI verifies size and SHA-256 on
every access and stages complete bytes before publishing them. For the
image datasets it is a directory: "mnist" and "fashion_mnist" hold the four uncompressed
IDX files (C<train-images-idx3-ubyte>, ...); "cifar10" holds C<data_batch_1..5.bin> and
C<test_batch.bin>; "cifar100" holds C<train.bin> and C<test.bin> (the binary versions);
"sudoku" holds Norvig's C<easy50.txt>, C<top95.txt> and C<hardest.txt>.
"karate_club" holds the970-byte original ZIP, GML topology and source README;
every cached archive/member is checksum-verified. karate_club() reads34nodes/78edges.
"rebot_devarm" holds 38 pinned Seeed DevArm CAD/URDF/STL files and the
CERN-OHL-W-2.0 source license in their upstream relative directory layout.
DevArm verifies the size and SHA-256 of every cached file on every call;
changed files throw without replacement. Missing files are staged and verified
before publication. It uses the same offline/mirror/cache controls, and works
without the optional native data-preparation dependencies. Hashing uses memory
proportional to the largest source file (about 35 MB).
Approximate download sizes: diamonds 2.7 MB, california_housing 1.4 MB, MNIST 11 MB,
Fashion-MNIST 30 MB, CIFAR-10 163 MB, CIFAR-100 161 MB, sudoku 14 KB, DevArm 56 MB.

B<Example>

    const auto housing = dm::datasets::read_csv(dm::datasets::fetch("california_housing"));

For a complete CAD asset tree, use C<dm::datasets::fetch("rebot_devarm")>.

B<References>

=over 4

=item *

Seeed reBot-DevArm source: https://github.com/Seeed-Projects/reBot-DevArm

=back

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$directory = ''>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$name> (string)

One of downloadable() or a registered UCI alias.

=item C<$directory> (string, optional)

Where the files live; empty means C<data_home() + "/" + name>. Files already present there are used as they are, except UCI, DevArm and karate_club's verified files.

=back

Returns string: The local path of the CSV file or the dataset directory.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): for an unknown name.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::runtime_error>): if files are missing and downloading is disabled or fails, or a download does not match its checksum.

See also: C<data_home()>, C<downloadable()>, C<download_file()>, C<karate_club()>.

=cut

sub fetch {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(115, [@_]);
}

=head2 download_file

    download_file($url, $destination, $md5);

Downloads C<url> to C<destination> with curl, unless the destination already exists.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::datasets::download_file>.

The file is downloaded into a temporary directory next to C<destination>, checked, and only
then renamed into place. Parent directories are created as needed. C<DATAMUNGE_DATA_OFFLINE>
is honored; C<DATAMUNGE_DATA_MIRROR> is not (fetch() applies it).

B<Example>

    dm::datasets::download_file("https://example.org/data.csv", "/tmp/data.csv");

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$md5 = ''>.

