Second line first point.

=item C<$p4> (Datamunge::Point2D)

Second line second point.

=item C<$out> (Datamunge::Point2D)

Borrowed output, assigned only on successful construction.

=back

Returns boolean: True when a finite approximate unique intersection was constructed.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): Nonfinite coordinate.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Arithmetic> (C++ C<std::overflow_error>): Nonzero quotient or final coordinate exceeds finite represented range.

See also: C<segment_intersection_point()>.

