=head2 draw_line

    draw_line($img, $x0, $y0, $x1, $y1, $color, $thickness);

Draws a straight line from (x0,y0) to (x1,y1) directly onto C<img> (Bresenham's
integer algorithm). C<thickness> E<gt> 1 stamps a (thickness x thickness) square at
every line pixel -- simple, not a true round/mitered stroke, but sufficient for this
module's scope. Points (and any square stamps) outside C<img's> bounds are silently
clipped rather than throwing, matching typical drawing-library behavior for
partially-offscreen shapes.

