=head2 levene_test

    my $result = levene_test($values, $group_sizes, $median_center);

Tests group scale with Levene's mean or Brown–Forsythe's median centering.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::stats::levene_test>.

Runs one-way ANOVA on absolute within-group deviations. Independent observations
and comparable group distribution shapes support interpreting the result as a scale test.

B<Example>

    const auto fit = dm::stats::levene_test({1, 2, 4, 3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 3, 4, 5, 5}, {3, 5, 4});
    std::print("{:.3f}\n", fit.statistic); // 3.550

B<References>

=over 4

=item *

Brown and Forsythe (1974), Robust Tests for the Equality of Variances,
doi:10.1080/01621459.1974.10482955.

=item *

https://docs.scipy.org/doc/scipy/reference/generated/scipy.stats.levene.html

=back

Arguments left out take the C++ defaults: C<$median_center = true>.

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$values> (array reference of number)

Finite observations concatenated by group.

=item C<$group_sizes> (array reference of integer)

At least two groups of size two or larger partitioning values.

=item C<$median_center> (boolean, optional)

Use group medians when true (default), or group means when false.

=back

Returns Datamunge::HypothesisTestResult: F statistic, two degrees of freedom and an approximate upper-tail p-value.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): Invalid inputs, zero residual deviation variance or overflow.

See also: C<bartlett_test()>, C<fligner_killeen_test()>.

