Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$events1> (integer)

Number of events from the first exposure.

=item C<$exposure1> (number)

Positive finite first exposure.

=item C<$events2> (integer)

Number of events from the second exposure.

=item C<$exposure2> (number)

Positive finite second exposure, in the same units.

=item C<$confidence_level> (number, optional)

Two-sided nominal coverage in (0,1), default .95.

=back

Returns Datamunge::PoissonRateInterval: First rate divided by the second and its interval. Zero events in both exposures give an absent estimate and the interval [0,+infinity].

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): Invalid exposure or confidence level.

See also: C<poisson_rate_interval()>.

