=head2 load

    my $result = load($name);

Any table-shaped dataset by name, e.g. "wine", like scikit-learn's C<fetch_openml()>
lookup by name.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::data::load>.

Accepts every name listed by catalog() whose storage is a table, bundled or downloaded
(a downloaded dataset is cached as described at datasets::load()).

B<Example>

    const std::unique_ptr<dm::DataFrame> wine(dm::data::load("wine"));
    std::print("{} x {}\n", wine->nrows(), wine->ncols());   // 178 x 14

Parameters:

=over 4

=item C<$name> (string)

A dataset name from catalog(), e.g. "iris" or "diamonds".

=back

Returns Datamunge::DataFrame or undef: A new DataFrame owned by the caller.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::InvalidArgument> (C++ C<std::invalid_argument>): for an unknown name, an image dataset's name or karate_club.

Dies with C<Datamunge::Error::Native> (C++ C<std::runtime_error>): if a downloaded dataset is not cached and cannot be fetched.

See also: C<catalog()>, C<datasets::load()>.

=cut

sub load {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(265, [@_]);
}

=head2 catalog

    my $result = catalog();

One row per available dataset: C<name>, C<rows>, C<columns>, C<storage>, C<size_mb> and
C<description>, like R's C<data()> listing.

Calls C++ C<datamunge::data::catalog>.

B<Example>

    const std::unique_ptr<dm::DataFrame> all(dm::data::catalog());
    std::print("{}\n", all->columns());   // ["name", "rows", "columns", "storage", "size_mb", "description"]

Returns Datamunge::DataFrame or undef: A new DataFrame owned by the caller.

See also: C<load()>, C<datasets::catalog()>.

=cut

sub catalog {
    return Datamunge::Rosetta::call(266, [@_]);
}

our @EXPORT_OK = qw(iris penguins tooth_growth wine titanic eight_schools air_passengers volcano faithful mtcars airquality breast_cancer diabetes digits diamonds california_housing load catalog);
our %EXPORT_TAGS = (all => \@EXPORT_OK);

